{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question","id":655261,"title":"Lucifuge's Demons (and a 2E update question)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-07T10:11:28-07:00","id":655261,"title":"Lucifuge's Demons (and a 2E update question)","content":"A pretty straight-forward question: Does it ever say which Demons the Lucifuge summons or gain their power from? Are they from Inferno, or one of the many places Mages refer to as Lower Depths? Obviously there's some headcanon available here (for source of power, I'd probably go for Inferno demons who had &quot;have intercourse with me&quot; as part of a pact they made with a female mortal, and thus Inferno for what demons they summon). Obviously Hunter is mildly less. . .cross-over friendly when it comes to metaphysics and cosmology, so I also wouldn't be surprised if it never really says.<br /> <br /> For the 2E question: Are there any general guidelines for translating powers? Specifically I'm looking at Family Vestment's ability to grant Armor 5, which is pretty intense. And, I suppose, Benedictions 'Armor of St. [Someone]' which can give Armor 5 as well. It's not really a problem to wing it myself, but I figured I'd look to see if there were hard and fast rules/guidelines for such a thing.<br /> <br /> Also, whoever changed how Elixers worked in Mortal Remains: thank you so very much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T10:33:43-07:00","id":655300,"title":"","content":"inferno is the lower depths, and yes presumably it is the inferno. then again, there are like 9 different things all called demons, so its up to you if its the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7141-nasrudin","name":"Nasrudin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7141_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T10:34:58-07:00","id":655302,"title":"","content":"Hah, yeah, sorry, that's what I meant: Inferno, or one of the OTHER Lower Depths. Sorry for being less than clear there. But thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T10:39:23-07:00","id":655308,"title":"","content":"IMO the tone of the Lucifuge's powers fits the Inferno too well to make it anything else. Not to mention that Inferno refers to the Lucifuge at at least two points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T10:43:05-07:00","id":655310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question#post655261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A pretty straight-forward question: Does it ever say which Demons the Lucifuge summons or gain their power from?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really! The demons of Hunter: the Vigil are an ambiguous presentation of various devilish phenomena, sometimes resembling the Inferno, once in awhile resembling the God-Machine angels or something else. The Inferno is the closest single fit, and the Inferno book presents the Lucifuge's rivals, the Children of the Seventh Generation, as an associated phenomenon. But overall, Hunter's demons are as well defined as Hunter's witches, which are not necessarily <i>not</i> the Awakened, but certainly don't always match up one-to-one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T10:49:15-07:00","id":655314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=655308#post655308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Inferno refers to the Lucifuge at at least two points.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=655310#post655310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> the Inferno book presents the Lucifuge's rivals, the Children of the Seventh Generation, as an associated phenomenon.</div> </div> </div> </div>There we go. As close as we're going to get, I imagine! Thanks, both of you! Am hanging out at my local gaming store prepping for a game this weekend by reading a bunch of Lucifuge stuff for a new inductee to WoD and figured I'd ask on here while I read.<br /> <br /> Mortal Remains connecting Lucifuge to the Unchained suuuuure is interesting! I like the idea of Lucifuge herself being an Angel. What a neat concept.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T12:11:24-07:00","id":655382,"title":"","content":"I sincerely hope they keep the broad umbrella. One of the coolest things I ever did to scare the crap out of my players was having the a group of Lucifuge summon a True Fae and not even bat an eye at it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T12:21:25-07:00","id":655387,"title":"","content":"It's intentionally ambiguous. At my own table it's Inferno Dominions (who have the Manifest numina to be the physical Greater Demons). Their metaphysical link to Spirits, Ghosts, and Goetia (via Diaboli) is why Lucifuge powers work on the broader range of ephemera.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T13:36:11-07:00","id":655453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=655382#post655382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I sincerely hope they keep the broad umbrella. One of the coolest things I ever did to scare the crap out of my players was having the a group of Lucifuge summon a True Fae and not even bat an eye at it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I sincerly hope they don't.<br /> <br /> The Lucifuge summoning a True Fae is perfectly fine. The Lucifuge summoning a True Fae because True Fae are demons is immersion breaking. Either explicitly say that the Lucifuge's powers work on everything and give a justification for why inherited demonoic powers can summon True Fae or limit them to actual demons.<br /> <br /> It's not like Lucifuge need Castigation to summon a True Fae. Mortals can do it in the right circumstances, and as princes of Hell they've got no shortage of wealth to make turning up and playing nice in the Faerie's best interests. There's even authentic folklore that the Gentry have to pay tribute to hell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T01:06:20-07:00","id":656203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=655453#post655453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lucifuge summoning a True Fae is perfectly fine. The Lucifuge summoning a True Fae because True Fae are demons is immersion breaking. Either explicitly say that the Lucifuge's powers work on everything and give a justification for why inherited demonoic powers can summon True Fae or limit them to actual demons.<br /> <br /> It's not like Lucifuge need Castigation to summon a True Fae. Mortals can do it in the right circumstances, and as princes of Hell they've got no shortage of wealth to make turning up and playing nice in the Faerie's best interests. There's even authentic folklore that the Gentry have to pay tribute to hell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends... I could certainly run a game in which True Fae are actually the demons from Inferno or as an explanation for most of those type of entities (other worldly types making deals and seducing mortals). It is not something that fits the standard nWoD, but if you want a cleaner less crowded world it certainly works. Keeping things a bit vague help individual storytellers adapt the setting to their tastes, so that is a good thing. It is not as if for most campaigns it is going to matter all that much...<br /> <br /> Note that folklore, Gentry and devils is a bit of a mixed bag, since Christianity had a reason to both demonify and lessen the power of the old gods which as a result eventually became both gentry and devils in folklore. Fact is that in folklore there is not nearly as clear a seperation between the various supernatural entities as within the core splat books.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T04:51:10-07:00","id":656383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madfox11</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=656203#post656203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends... I could certainly run a game in which True Fae are actually the demons from Inferno or as an explanation for most of those type of entities (other worldly types making deals and seducing mortals). It is not something that fits the standard nWoD, but if you want a cleaner less crowded world it certainly works.</div> </div> </div> </div>Certainly you could, but I think the point stands because in such a case you'd be admitting the Fae into the ranks of the Lucifuge's ancestors. But the background of the Lucifuge posits them as the descendants of a particular type of being - or even a specific individual within it - so I do think it's worth specifying (for a chronicle if not the for the books) which entities they are, and limiting the banishing/binding and familiar abilities to those alone.<br /> <br /> I've heard the argument that that's too limiting on those powers, but I don't buy that - a lot of Endowment powers are only useful against one type of creature, and the Lucifuge have plenty of Castigations that function more widely.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T09:44:12-07:00","id":656630,"title":"","content":"all the thing about the Lucifuge is kinda confusing for a number of reasons-<br /> <br /> a) Hunter's Demons are a broad category of many different beings hunters usually lump under a single title (like they usually do)<br /> b) Castigations are described to effect many different beings <b>including </b>Hunter's Demons, which makes things even more confusing about their origin.<br /> c) After Inferno, most agree that the Lucifuge's lineage come from a single, definitive origin (Inferno)<br /> <br /> In sort, the reason for all of the debates and confusion comes from the fact that a later (none Hunter, even) book came, and it was cool enough to accept what it had to offer (unlike other blue books which shall not be named). Actually, I've talked about the subject once, when it looked strange to me that beings who gain their powers from Inferno could command and make contact with the Abyss, for each of the realms kinda see the other as a natural enemy.<br /> <br /> Now, there are a number of options for this. The first is that because the chances are that most of the confusion and contradiction about what a &quot;demon&quot; is come from early material meeting new material, Hunter's 2nd Edition may change how Castigations work. I'm not sure how I feel about that option, and it is not relevant for now- so let's skip it. The other option is ignoring Inferno and keeping the Lucifuge's origin as mystery- which is even harder to do, since you can't put the genei back in the bottle. The third option is start making explanations for how Castigations work- which may stretch Suspension of Disbelief a bit. I mean, if you had one explanation for everything it may have worked- but there isn't. You gonna make a number of explanations, each per being which may be effected by Castigations: Spirits+Ghosts+Geotia? It is Inferno's corruption. True Fae? They can't be corrupted by Hell, so let's use the &quot;tribute to Hell&quot;. Abyss? their demon parents has made them into some sort of living weapons. Supernal Demons? they resonate with the concept of Sin? Descent's Demons?....<br /> <br /> In sort, too many explanations- unless you tie everything to Hell, which can work only for some games.<br /> <br /> The last option (which I use for now) is that there is a difference between being a Child of 7th Generation and actually knowing Castigations. The first is your origin- you have certain properties because of your lineage, and have some potential to do cool things. Castigations, however, are things you learn- they are rites discovered by the Lady which you imprint upon your soul and connect it to Hell. The fact that you can manipulate your soul to do some weird and terrible things which it shouldn't do (even by the standards of those who created you) is something which is really a part of being an hunter. Your demon ancestors didn't meant you to command Hell, the Abyss and the Fae all as one- but you do, and you do it without even understanding why what you do is <i>wrong</i>. Sure, those are unnatural rites which taint all that is holy- but you are an unnatural being who taints all that is holy by yourself. There is nothing special here, no matter what your pet demon is telling to you. Well, maybe it is a bit weird. Maybe you should check it out. Maybe the Lady has some answers..<br /> <br /> In sort, you are an hunter, and hunters do all kinds of weird things which breaks the delicate cosmologies of other gamelines. Have fun!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T10:53:00-07:00","id":656731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=656630#post656630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">a) Hunter's Demons are a broad category of many different beings hunters usually lump under a single title (like they usually do)</div> </div> </div> </div> Which kind of bugs me. If there's one group in the WoD who <b>wouldn't</b> lump different things togeather it's Hunters. We all know what happens when a Hunter whips out holy water against the Changeling who looks like a horned red guy. The Hunter dies.<br /> <br /> Obviously competence varies and nobody has an accurate map of the WoD cosmos. But you can't ignore the fact that what Hunters want and need is accurate ways to say what powers this monster has and what kind of bullets will hurt it.<br /> <br /> Even the Malleus Maleficarum have an entire Order who's philosophy amounts to &quot;figure out how to fight it now and worry about how this fits with The Bible later&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=656630#post656630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">b) Castigations are described to effect many different beings <b>including </b>Hunter's Demons, which makes things even more confusing about their origin.</div> </div> </div> </div> Not to mention that the choice of which beings doesn't make much sense.<br /> <br /> Infernal Demons and Unchained Demons are included; but True Fae are not. The Inferno has much more in common with the Gentry than with the Unchained.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=656630#post656630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hunter's 2nd Edition may change how Castigations work.</div> </div> </div> </div> It probably will. Look at Seitokuken - it mentions both demons and spirits. 1E Castigation treats Demons as a form of Spirit.<br /> <br /> I approve of this direction. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=656630#post656630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Castigations, however, are things you learn- they are rites discovered by the Lady which you imprint upon your soul and connect it to Hell.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is probably going to be the case - but IMO it conflicts with the whole lineage theme at the core of the Lucifuge. Ah well <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T13:34:12-07:00","id":656860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=656731#post656731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Which kind of bugs me. If there's one group in the WoD who <b>wouldn't</b> lump different things togeather it's Hunters. We all know what happens when a Hunter whips out holy water against the Changeling who looks like a horned red guy. The Hunter dies.<br /> <br /> Obviously competence varies and nobody has an accurate map of the WoD cosmos. But you can't ignore the fact that what Hunters want and need is accurate ways to say what powers this monster has and what kind of bullets will hurt it.<br /> <br /> Even the Malleus Maleficarum have an entire Order who's philosophy amounts to &quot;figure out how to fight it now and worry about how this fits with The Bible later&quot;.<br /> <br /> Not to mention that the choice of which beings doesn't make much sense.<br /> <br /> Infernal Demons and Unchained Demons are included; but True Fae are not. The Inferno has much more in common with the Gentry than with the Unchained.</div> </div> </div> </div>What hunters <b>shouldn't</b> do what what they <b>don't</b> do are completely different things. At the end of the day, most supernatural communities don't even really know what the hell (hah) is going on, and they've got things going for them like &quot;supernatural ways to find things out&quot;, &quot;not dying in droves while pursuing the Vigil&quot;, and sometimes &quot;we don't age, making a running Oral History far easier&quot;. There are exceptions, of course -- the Malleus group you mentioned is a fantastic example of how a group of Hunters, with the proper mindset and roots in a long-term organization like The Vatican, can do better than basically guess at what's what. But they're clearly the exception.<br /> <br /> The True Fae might have more in common with Inferno and the Unchained, but the True Fae are WAY out there in terms of obfuscation. They're the boogie-man to a group of people that are notoriously hard to track down and are among the most paranoid of splats.<br /> <br /> That being said, I do hope (and, based on a few posts/lines, expect) Hunter2 will be more consolidated in how it functions and what it tells the players. That being said, I dearly hope that the confusion of what's what when it comes to the Hunt is still present, because it'd be pretty weird if it wasn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T15:32:43-07:00","id":657025,"title":"","content":"So what happens when a hunter tosses water on a horned red changeling....who has a frailty to holy water? The Hunter lives.<br /> So what happens when that hunter goes and talks to the rest of the cell of the hunter who died trying the exact same thing? Confusion, and any number of answers from there.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I find the assertion that hunters don't lump things together to be absurd, and it was one of my biggest problems with Mortal Remains. Hunters aren't in a position to see the big picture, and this is why they make a lot of the choices they end up making. The phrase &quot;When all you have is a hammer, everything starts looking like a nail&quot; is always true for hunters. Consider that this is a group where almost every single on of them has a baseline answer to most problems in the form of &quot;Destroy the head and set it on fire&quot;. Yes, they seem like they are in a better position to understand things that the supernatural themselves-they aren't deeply involved with a supernatural model of reality, and thus can compare things. But the big problem with this assumption is what a <i>lack</i> of a pre-existing model does. The templates know a little something, and it's easier for them to see what is not because they know their lines. Hunters, by contrast, have to string things along case by case, and in that situation, it's easier to base things on what works them rather than what they actually are. That's all before you go into the aforementioned fact that each group has their own bases and models they try and shove everything into If any group is, in reality, likely to get your demony goodness in my gooey changeling, it's hunters.<br /> <br /> In a similar vein, I dislike the assertion that the Lucifuge and L'Enfant Diabolique draw from strictly the Inferno.(And yes, I read the section in Inferno) The sidebar in the first Hunter binding a bunch of disparate portions of the other gamelines under their umbrella together created a great iconic base that also asked some great questions and created a great setting mystery for players to answer that. It made them a collection of dark and fallen families embracing one another under the same idea expressed by a very powerful mythos, like a proto-Beast Family ideal. It was compelling because it challenged assertions, which is what the World of Darkness is all about-the fact that you can dig and dig and dig and never find the answer.<br /> <br /> That was always fascinating to me. Yes, I like playing the prince of hell, but I like playing a prince of darkness who never quite knows what he'll find when he turn the rock over better. But I've had this argument with Raven before and it never goes anywhere. Us thinking the other is wrong is nothing new.<br /> <br /> PS: For the record, in reference to the sidebar and on what Castigation affects, the books says &quot;Most hunters don\u2019t know (or care) enough to distinguish fallen angels of the Pit, spirits from the spirit world, unnatural blasphemies from the Abyss, or bizarre nightmares from the realm of dreams.&quot; Given the way the word play in Hunter works as well as Dancers in the Dusk not being out yet, I don't see how people can't read that last one as being the True Fae, so that entire &quot;Castigations don't affect True Fae&quot; doesn't make a lick of sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T17:48:35-07:00","id":657210,"title":"","content":"Couldn't &quot;bizarre nightmares etc&quot; bit be a reference to Astral entities, since there are entities therein referee to as Demons (whatever the manifestations of your sins or whatever are called. Goetica?). I'm not opposed to Castigations working on True Fae - them working on any extraplanar entity is pretty alright with me, really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T00:13:20-07:00","id":657461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=656860#post656860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What hunters <b>shouldn't</b> do what what they <b>don't</b> do are completely different things.</div> </div> </div> </div> I disagree. The question isn't shouldn't vs don't. The question is sucecss vs failure.<br /> <br /> The vast vast majority of Hunters will try to find out what kind of monster they're facing and what weapons work against them. They might get it wrong, it's <i>hard</i> to tell the difference between a demon and a red horned changeling if they don't want you to know the truth - but the hunters will still try.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=657025#post657025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what happens when a hunter tosses water on a horned red changeling....who has a frailty to holy water? The Hunter lives.<br /> So what happens when that hunter goes and talks to the rest of the cell of the hunter who died trying the exact same thing? Confusion, and any number of answers from there.</div> </div> </div> </div> Again. Monster classification is hard.<br /> <br /> You can bet your bottom dollar though, that Hunters will <i>try</i> to find some reliable way of telling which red horned monsters are hurt by holy water and which monsters are immune.<br /> <br /> They might not succeed in creating a classification system but they will try. Even when they get it wrong, hunter's do <u>care</u>. The sidebar is wrong.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=657025#post657025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The phrase &quot;When all you have is a hammer, everything starts looking like a nail&quot; is always true for hunters.</div> </div> </div> </div> Absolutely not. Hunters do not have a hammer. Plenty of monsters are bullet proof. Hunters who use the same tactics against every monster are going to die.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T01:18:49-07:00","id":657514,"title":"","content":"I'm not saying they don't TRY to classify monsters correctly, I'm saying they very often fail due to a large number of factors. Clearly only the most foolish of Hunters are going to sniff out a monster just to ignore any hints they've been getting as to it's nature and go in guns blazing, but there's simply too much shit out there for the vast majority of Hunter Cells (only Tier 3 Hunters really have a shot, imo, and even then only when they belong to specific Conspiracies and/or subfactions) to really have a handle on the finer points of cosmology. Vampires vs. Werewolves? Sure. Pretty easy. &quot;Is this thing a Demon from Inferno or a summoned Supernal being from Pandemonium&quot; is. . .a little over the top. Hell, one of the earlier examples -- True Fae as Demon versus Unchained as Demon -- requires a situation in which the Hunter Cell has <i>run in to both of those things and been able to figure out what the really are</i>. Without dying. Or being mind-raped.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T01:35:43-07:00","id":657538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=657514#post657514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IHell, one of the earlier examples -- True Fae as Demon versus Unchained as Demon -- requires a situation in which the Hunter Cell has <i>run in to both of those things and been able to figure out what the really are</i>. Without dying. Or being mind-raped.</div> </div> </div> </div>And even then they have to actually observe them in a situation where the differences come into actual play, which can be pretty hard for people who have no special powers related to said entities. Although admittedly, True Fae are going to be notoriously hard to identify. Each one is different from another, even their weaknesses vary with cold iron being the unified one (but that is actually a weaknesses of demons in folklore as well).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T09:33:51-07:00","id":658010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=657461#post657461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They might not succeed in creating a classification system but they will try. Even when they get it wrong, hunter's do <u>care</u>. The sidebar is wrong.<br /> <br /> Absolutely not. Hunters do not have a hammer. Plenty of monsters are bullet proof. Hunters who use the same tactics against every monster are going to die.</div> </div> </div> </div>0) Wow, okay, tell the writers and developer of the time they are wrong. Tell everyone who wrote the books and kept that as canon as wrong. What a fucking terrible attitude.<br /> <br /> 1) They do have classification systems. The Lucifuge has one where their powers work on Infernal demons, Unchained demons, spirits, Abyssal entitites, and True Fae. They categorize everything that Castigation works on as a demon, and since it works for them, it's right for them. Does this mean that the Knights of Saint Adrian or Les Mysteres or Knights of Saint George agree? Some might, most would not-but they can't argue the results of their Castigations, which brings me to....<br /> <br /> 2) Abso-fucking-lutely hunters have 'hammers'. When holy water works the first time on something, you make damned sure to see if it works again, particularly when that's the only thing you know of that does. Hunters are limited by knowledge,and until their knowledge is proven wrong, they'll rely on what they know to work. The ideas of compilations of various methods comes from years of going through the process of working on the original models of understanding until it's broken and requires a new model. In the process, hunters can and will have factually fault models that nevertheless work for them. It gets more complicated when those hunters embrace powers that defy the normal rules of functions, but so long as the model answers the questions, hunters don't stress too much about the details. Most of the conspiracies(Oh hey, significance of that word again) are at this point, where they have a model that answers for most everything they'll come across and makes unusual cases easy to not worry about, Once those cases gain mass and break the model, then they might revise it, but for them, it'll take centuries to do.<br /> <br /> Sorry if you don't like it, but people are building a horror mystery game here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-09-2015, 12:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T09:47:14-07:00","id":658040,"title":"","content":"Like, why the fuck would you ever say the sidebar is wrong? What, do you think the development team literally just threw that out there, like someone wrote it, and Chuck Wendig went &quot;Well, fuck, that's stupid, but we're on such a tight schedule we'll have to keep that in.&quot;, like Chuck, <i>of all people</i>, would just let that sit in there? What the fuck? How can anyone think that? It's incredibly stupid to think the people making this book are wrong, because, hello, it's their book.<br /> <br /> Seriously, I'm flat out baffled by that assertion. It's ludicrous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T10:03:19-07:00","id":658059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=657514#post657514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not saying they don't TRY to classify monsters correctly, I'm saying they very often fail due to a large number of factors.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then we agree <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=658040#post658040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like, why the fuck would you ever say the sidebar is wrong?</div> </div> </div> </div>Simple. It is contradicted by the rest of the setting.<br /> <br /> It says Hunters don't care about the difference between, e.g. infernal demons and True Fae. Everything else in the Hunter gameline says that hunters have to care because if they bring the wrong weapons they're dead.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=658010#post658010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) Abso-fucking-lutely hunters have 'hammers'. When holy water works the first time on something, you make damned sure to see if it works again</div> </div> </div> </div> And when you try it to see if it works again, 99 times out of 100 it won't.<br /> <br /> Hunters would love to have a hammer, but barring a Vigil exclusively focused on one type of monster there isn't a single weapon or Tactic (including Endowments) in the WoD that works against the majority of monsters. (Unless you use the fire kills everything hack in Armoury Reloaded)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 09-09-2015, 01:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T14:58:20-07:00","id":658426,"title":"","content":"In hindsight 'bizarre nightmares from the realm of dreams&quot; sounds a lot like Beast's 'Horrors' from the Primordial Dream. Obviously it didn't exist when the line was written, but it's an interesting angle to think about.<br /> <br /> I've always ruled that Lucifuge abilities work on anything I would generally consider an 'outsider'. Inferno Demons, Spirits, Ghosts, Fae, Abyssal Entities, Supernal Creatures. Using them on Unchained and Angels has never come up in my game, but I don't see them as outsiders per se.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-09T15:45:59-07:00","id":658523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=658059#post658059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Simple. It is contradicted by the rest of the setting.<br /> <br /> It says Hunters don't care about the difference between, e.g. infernal demons and True Fae. Everything else in the Hunter gameline says that hunters have to care because if they bring the wrong weapons they're dead.<br /> <br /> And when you try it to see if it works again, 99 times out of 100 it won't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Blessing your bullets or melee weapons by coating them with Holy Water before a fight not only isn't going to get you killed, but will be terribly hard to determine if it isn't working as well. How can you tell if your holy water isn't harming them as much as it did the last thing you fought, or if this thing is just tougher? Especially in the middle of a fight, which isn't the standard place for calm, collected thoughts? Even amongst the same group of things -- maybe you got lucky on your first Hunt and that Vampire had a Bane involving Holy Water. Now you're fighting this OTHER Vampire and. . .your weapons don't seem as effective. Does the Holy Water thing not work? Does this Vampire simply have a decent number of dots in Resilience? Wait, aren't there some God-fearing branch of Vampires? Maybe Holy Water doesn't work against them specifically. Hard to tell. But it's not costing you anything -- just make sure you go to Mass every Sunday (or have a great excuse not to) and the good Father is willing to give you as much Holy Water as you need. And, really, praying over your weapons and rubbing some Holy Water on them isn't exactly cutting in to your free time.<br /> <br /> The only thing that will surefire kill you is being cocky -- and that'll happen even if you DO have the perfect weapon for the job.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=658059#post658059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hunters would love to have a hammer, but barring a Vigil exclusively focused on one type of monster there isn't a single weapon or Tactic (including Endowments) in the WoD that works against the majority of monsters. (Unless you use the fire kills everything hack in Armoury Reloaded)</div> </div> </div> </div>That's. . .really not true. Guns and machetes work against most everything. It sometimes works less well against certain things (Vampires, as an obvious example) but they still work. And, really, even without the Fire Kills Everything hack. . .fire kills most everything.For Endowments: Malleus' Wrathful Sword of St. Michael, Lucifuge's Hellfire, Ascending One's Blood of the Cobra, Knights of Saint Adrian's The Lord Provides and Bear Mace, Aegis Kai Doru's Doru Talisman, Les Mysteres' Wearing the Baron's Hat, Cheiron Group's Vitriol Pump. . all of those work against most monsters.As far as Tactics, I'm not sure, as I'm not terribly interested in those (they might just not have clicked with me yet, but I'm hoping something fun is done with them in Hunter2).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T01:12:20-07:00","id":659092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=658523#post658523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blessing your bullets or melee weapons by coating them with Holy Water before a fight not only isn't going to get you killed, but will be terribly hard to determine if it isn't working as well.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes you can bless every gun you have. It wouldn't hurt. You could go further: Buckshot filled with silver, cold iron, napalm, metorite dust, communion wafers, and everything you can think of.<br /> <br /> But do you know what I'd call a hunter who did that and said that's good enough? I'd call them cocky.<br /> <br /> There's always a (fairly high) chance that this monster is the one that's immune to <b>all</b> the banes you've packed in. And when that happens, you're right, a cocky hunter is a dead hunter.<br /> <br /> In short. A hunter still has to <u>care</u>. Because no matter how many banes they pack into one shell of buckshot - they still should research their prey and do their best to find out what it is and make damn sure they have the right weapons, because they're betting their life on it.<br /> <br /> <br /> And don't forget that hunter's have more weapons than just guns. Even with both cold iron and silver in a buckshot shell you're still at a massive disadvantage if you confuse the Changeling with Fang and Talon for a Werewolf. One of a Hunter's most potent weapons is Tactics (and small t tactics). Trying to make a werewolf rage so it becomes predictable and stupid is a valid Tactic, but a changeling would probably laugh it off.<br /> <br /> Even if you can get every bane into a gun - say an AKD relic with the power of &quot;always shoots the bullets most harmful to the target&quot; a Hunter still has to <u>care</u> what kind of monster they're up against. Because they might be up against a Vampire with Clarity and if they don't have a plan to counter super-speed that gun's going to be useless when the vampire effortlessly dodges every bullet. Or a Mask Slasher where the bullet &quot;most harmful&quot; is a regular bullet and &quot;most harmful&quot; is &quot;only one Lethal damage&quot;.<br /> <br /> So knowing what you're up against is still vital. Hunter's still have to care what kind of a monster they're facing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=658523#post658523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's. . .really not true. Guns and machetes work against most everything.</div> </div> </div> </div> Clearly we're using a different definition of &quot;work&quot;. When I say work I mean &quot;will kill the monster without too many Hunter's dying&quot;.<br /> <br /> Simply charging into the monster's lair guns blazing or swinging the Warthful Sword of St. Michael is not going to create a successful long term Vigil. Blood of the Cobra is powerful and never hurts (unless you fail the activation roll) but in of itself it is not sufficent. You still need to combine it with knowledge of what monster you're up against and a strategy to bypass their strengths and exploit their weaknesses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 09-10-2015, 10:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T01:34:29-07:00","id":659106,"title":"","content":"Huh? Getting something angry to the point of it ignoring common sense always works. It is certainly a common trope in stories. Of course, you better have something on your sleeves to take advantage of said rage, because otherwise you will be just as dead. Your example only highlights the fact that many tactics work against all opponents, they just happen to be more or less effective or easier to pull off against one set of monsters, but not another. What is more, unless you run across a lot of wolf-like changelings (assuming you can even see it is a wolf-like changeling because that is doubtful), you are just as likely to assume to have run across a werewolf with a strong willpower than that it is a completely different creature, especially since that Changeling is going to be just as hurt as a werewolf when hit by silver bullets or a large bonfire <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T03:07:19-07:00","id":659165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madfox11</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=659106#post659106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh? Getting something angry to the point of it ignoring common sense always works.</div> </div> </div> </div> It's a common trope in stories but it's typically used against charachters who're already eastablished to have temper as a weakness. There's plenty of stories where trying to get someone angry doesn't work at all. Avatar the Last Airbender Boiling Rock part 2 for example.<br /> <br /> Werewolves have Death Rage and Vampires have Frenzy. Changelings have neither. This isn't just my opinion. The Bait and Switch tactic in Spirit Slayers only mentions those two monsters. Now if I were ST I would allow you to use it on other monsters that have anger issues unrelated to their splat but if you go around using it on every random Changeling, most of the time it won't work at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madfox11</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=659106#post659106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, you better have something on your sleeves to take advantage of said rage</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course. I suggest the roadkill Tactic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madfox11</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=659106#post659106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">you are just as likely to assume to have run across a werewolf with a strong willpower than that it is a completely different creature</div> </div> </div> </div> Perhaps. And then you're in trouble.<br /> <br /> Hunters get monsters mixed up all the time. Classifying monsters is hard. But that doesn't stop them from <i>trying</i>. Their lives are on the line, they care deeply about correctly classifying monsters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 09-10-2015, 06:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T05:50:59-07:00","id":659270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=659165#post659165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hunters get monsters mixed up all the time. Classifying monsters is hard. But that doesn't stop them from <i>trying</i>. Their lives are on the line, they care deeply about correctly classifying monsters.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think we are debating that is not the case. It is only human nature after all. What we are debating is its effectiveness in practice, especially when it comes to specific banes. After all, you and I know enough about the setting to realize there is a difference between a darkling changeling draining the energy of somebody or a vampire. The Hunter will not, at least not at first sight, and unless he comes across a lot of changelings, he is never going to realize that it was anything else besides a vampire with odd powers. I certainly feel that Hunters just do not come across enough monsters for any meaningful classification, except a vague notion of the various creatures. Tier 3 hunters might have a better go at it, but they run across another problem: too many monsters with too widely different powers that makes classification hard. As a result, basing your hunting tactics on any classification is just as dangerous as using none. It just helps you narrow the field a bit from the start.<br /> <br /> Mind you, it has nothing to do with the fact that the castigations apparently work against True Fae and other extra-dimensional threats. Although that might be more of a ruling to make the powers more fun for the players, since it would otherwise be rather limited in a typical Monster-of-the-Day campaign.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T05:51:27-07:00","id":659276,"title":"","content":"The question of why Lucifuge powers work on True Fae has a really obvious answer I'm surprised none of you brought up. <br /> <br /> They could have made a pact with them at some point. <br /> <br /> Which has the added bonus question of &quot;what did the Fae get out it?&quot; to answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T05:59:38-07:00","id":659290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=659276#post659276\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The question of why Lucifuge powers work on True Fae has a really obvious answer I'm surprised none of you brought up.<br /> <br /> They could have made a pact with them at some point.<br /> <br /> Which has the added bonus question of &quot;what did the Fae get out it?&quot; to answer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering the folklore of Fae paying tribute to Hell, I expect it as a &quot;Aw hell, Look, I know rent is not due today...&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh.. wait.. your not the boss.. You're his offspring.. hum.. I can have some fun with this...&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-10T06:36:04-07:00","id":659325,"title":"","content":"That's explored extensively in Dream Catchers <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> When I wrote that bit I designed it to promote maximum interaction between the True Fae and the Lucifuge, and between the Lucifuge and Changelings.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madfox11</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=659270#post659270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What we are debating is its effectiveness in practice, especially when it comes to specific banes.</div> </div> </div> </div> Um. Why are we debating that?<br /> <br /> I think we more or less agree about the effectiveness.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T01:18:22-07:00","id":660502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=659325#post659325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Um. Why are we debating that?<br /> <br /> I think we more or less agree about the effectiveness.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It started with hammers and everything looking like nails <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T09:20:02-07:00","id":660783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=657025#post657025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It made them a collection of dark and fallen families embracing one another under the same idea expressed by a very powerful mythos, like a proto-Beast Family ideal. It was compelling because it challenged assertions, which is what the World of Darkness is all about-the fact that you can dig and dig and dig and never find the answer.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Never any answers&quot; is something that can be overdone, and I think this would be a case of it. Especially as Castigation is in the blood, which implies the blood coming from a particular source. Now if you want to say &quot;what is it about this source that gives it power over X, Y, and Z, but not W or U, and I'm not certain about V,&quot; then that's a worthwhile plot hook - but saying they derive from many first causes that all happen manifest in the exact same way, and de facto coordinate with each other to keep the 666 total going, is vagueness, not mystery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T11:37:46-07:00","id":660931,"title":"","content":"There's a variety of reasons why the Lucifuge's Castigations work on a larger group than just demons.<br /> <br /> There is, as many have noted, the the longstanding association of many different kinds of entities through the word demon. There's the benefit of a broad mechanical base that doesn't limit them to just dealing with one kind of monster (coughcoughlookingatyouknightsofsaintgeorgecoughco ugh). There's greater iconic power from drawing from beyond the simplest source that help to keep their nature feeling strange and dangerous and not properly understood. There's not being so simple as to be droll(fuck, I need to say that again, <i>there's not being so simple as to be droll</i>). It emphasizes the depth and breadth of the World of Darkness while also emphaszing that all will never be known. It strongly emphasizes the many themes of the Lucifuge as a group, particularly in the area of not being able to trust what's within, both as an individual and as an organization. So on and so forth.<br /> <br /> These are things that matter. As always, instead of asking why they didn't do it our way, maybe we should be asking why they did it their way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T14:25:21-07:00","id":661075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=660931#post660931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As always, instead of asking why they didn't do it our way, maybe we should be asking why they did it their way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that directed to me or a general group which includes me?<br /> <br /> Because in that case I'd like to quote what I said way back on page one: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=655453#post655453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lucifuge summoning a True Fae is perfectly fine. The Lucifuge summoning a True Fae because True Fae are demons is immersion breaking. Either explicitly say that the Lucifuge's powers work on everything and give a justification for why inherited demonoic powers can summon True Fae or limit them to actual demons.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would be fine with Lucifuge having powers over the True Fae - if the write up explained why they do (and there's no shortage of material to work with).<br /> <br /> <br /> But this is all accedemic. 2E is coming and will change things up. Spirits and Demons are now clearly distinct in the Seitokuken rules. Thus the word &quot;demon&quot; can't mean &quot;anything otherworldly&quot;. I'm happy with this direction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T14:45:25-07:00","id":661118,"title":"","content":"just wants to mention that demon and spirit are already two separate things- the &quot;spirit template&quot; is given at Spirit Slayers and the &quot;demon template&quot; is in the core and expanded in Mortal Remains. &quot;demon&quot; is anything otherworldly only in context with Castigations, and while Castigations and Seitokuken are similar powers, they may have their differences. Now, I'm not saying that the way Castigations treat &quot;demons&quot; would not change in the next edition- only that we don't have any indication it would.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-11T16:53:21-07:00","id":661232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=661075#post661075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is that directed to me or a general group which includes me?<br /> <br /> Because in that case I'd like to quote what I said way back on page one:<br /> <br /> I would be fine with Lucifuge having powers over the True Fae - if the write up explained why they do (and there's no shortage of material to work with).<br /> <br /> <br /> But this is all accedemic. 2E is coming and will change things up. Spirits and Demons are now clearly distinct in the Seitokuken rules. Thus the word &quot;demon&quot; can't mean &quot;anything otherworldly&quot;. I'm happy with this direction.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) The general group.<br /> <br /> 2)It works because they have power over demons, which includes spirits and True Fae. It makes perfect sense from one angle and zero sense from another,and that's perfectly fine by me because it works either way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T04:15:04-07:00","id":661775,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=655453#post655453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I sincerly hope they don't.</div> </div> </div> </div></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=655453#post655453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">The Lucifuge summoning a True Fae is perfectly fine. The Lucifuge summoning a True Fae because True Fae are demons is immersion breaking. Either explicitly say that the Lucifuge's powers work on everything and give a justification for why inherited demonoic powers can summon True Fae or limit them to actual demons.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> The True Fae may as well be demons. They've been called that by even the Lost. The Gentry represent the Unseelie Fae (which have been demonized) to the Lost's Seelie Courts. </span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> There are legends of demon slayers using iron as their weapons - Shiva used an iron trident to slay demons in Hindu lore, for instance. In WoD terms, we know that story would have to refer to one of the Fae, but its still called a demon in the story. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Of course, all this is supposing 1e content. We don't know how the 2e Lucifuge will be portrayed. The intent of the game seems to be leaning away from having Infernal demons as main antagonists (definitely an impression I picked up in the Hunter Core) and moving to just all other monsters. 2e, in general, seems to be less than a good fit for the Infernal - the only real support that particular book has are the increasingly less relevant maeljin - no one in the Astral really touches on infernally tainted goetics, it didn't come up in the Underworld book or Geist, and even Werewolf 2e has pushed the maeljin to a lesser position than they were in the past. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's not like Lucifuge need Castigation to summon a True Fae. </div> </div> </div> The Lucifuge can deal with the Abyss through Castigation. The Abyss is specifically not related to the Infernal in 1e - they're rivals, not allies.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=656383#post656383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Certainly you could, but I think the point stands because in such a case you'd be admitting the Fae into the ranks of the Lucifuge's ancestors. But the background of the Lucifuge posits them as the descendants of a particular type of being - or even a specific individual within it - so I do think it's worth specifying (for a chronicle if not the for the books) which entities they are, and limiting the banishing/binding and familiar abilities to those alone.</div> </div> </div> </div> I can make arguments that the Lucifuge already includes wolfbloods and dhampirs into the bloodlines. So, why not? What's wrong with the Lucifuge including traces of anyone with supernatural ability into the Lucifuge, and teaching them Castigation is just a way of bringing out that latent monster-power laying dorment in their blood? Its a pretty cool way of seeing that all monsters are family (*Cough*Beast*cough*DarkMother*cough*). </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I've heard the argument that that's too limiting on those powers, but I don't buy that - a lot of Endowment powers are only useful against one type of creature, and the Lucifuge have plenty of Castigations that function more widely. </div> </div> </div> Said Endowments are found in the hunt-the-monster splat book; the Who Is Caine group hunts exclusively vampires. The Lucifuge are one of the core six, who hunt everything.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=656731#post656731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Which kind of bugs me. If there's one group in the WoD who <b>wouldn't</b> lump different things togeather it's Hunters. We all know what happens when a Hunter whips out holy water against the Changeling who looks like a horned red guy. The Hunter dies.</div> </div> </div> </div> Holy water doesn't work against anything in the WoD unless they have a specific frailty/bane to it. If the particular brand of holy water includes salt, its likely effective against ghosts (as per the salt rules in Rules Update). If that holy water was created by the God Machine (and thus actually &quot;holy&quot;) it likely could cause a Compromise check against demons. But those are all big ifs - not what most people assume is holy water. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Iron is a weakness of the fey, silver of werewolves, fire for vamps/prommies/mummies. Those three are pretty much the exhaustive list of banes you can count on. The Awakened don't have a bane, nor do the Bound, Unchained, or Begotten. Hunters might carry around some cold iron and silver and moltovs, but the rest of obscure things? &quot;Well, sometimes it works, but mostly it doesn't.&quot; For the most part, Hunters Compacts and Conspiracies would quickly realize that there's no rhyme or reason to weaknesses, and that would only encourage lumping more. If its a devil-themed fae, spirit, or ghost, chances are it has a traditionally &quot;holy&quot; weakness. Dragon-themed monsters tend to have Anathema, frailties, and banes that revolve around certain weapons, soft scales on belly, and kidnapping beautiful people. Doesn't matter if we're talking about one of the Children, fae, or whatever. </span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=657025#post657025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> Hunters aren't in a position to see the big picture, and this is why they make a lot of the choices they end up making. </span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> Curious minds inquiring - you feel the same way about the higher ups in the Conspiracies as well?</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=657461#post657461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I disagree. The question isn't shouldn't vs don't. The question is sucecss vs failure.</div> </div> </div> </div> That assumes a database of some kind. You'd be surprised how often, before the advent of computers to organize data, people repeated each other's mistakes in the fields. And hunters don't really organize data well - they're still mostly in the dark ages when it comes to monster research. That'll change as more and more information is digitalized, but its not a given at the moment.</span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> But I feel only the conspiracies have the time and knowledge to put such a database together, and I\u2019m not comfortable assuming a tier 3 game - I\u2019m more of a tier 1/2 girl.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The sidebar is wrong. </div> </div> </div> I'm sorry, but I draw the line at &quot;the setting as presented is wrong!&quot; Do what you want with your games, say you prefer other things, but don't call the established setting wrong. </span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">The writers get to decide the setting and how things work. Not you.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Absolutely not. Hunters do not have a hammer. Plenty of monsters are bullet proof. Hunters who use the same tactics against every monster are going to die. </div> </div> </div> Fire tends to kill anything with a corpreal body. </span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Armor piercing rounds tends to work - even in the WoD, there\u2019s no such thing as bullet proof. You can be bullet resistant, but not proof. So, enough bullets in the air WILL kill even a vampire with Resilience 5 and full SWAT body armor. Or a Beast with Lair 10 and armor-granting Atavism. Even ephemeral beings who Materialize can be brought down that way. Might not be the most effective means, but its possible. </span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=658059#post658059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">Simple. It is contradicted by the rest of the setting.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">It says Hunters don't care about the difference between, e.g. infernal demons and True Fae. Everything else in the Hunter gameline says that hunters have to care because if they bring the wrong weapons they're dead.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> No, that's not a contradiction. That's you making assumptions. Hunters have to care, yes. But the assumption hunters have the time and ability to figure out the right weapons is a stretch. Furthermore, you're assuming that the infernal demon won't have a Bane or Ban related to iron as well, or that a True Fae won't have some resistance to iron like vamps can use Resilience to shrug off fire, or wolves use Rage Gift armor to ignore silver bullets. From a hunter perspective, even using Iron against the fae isn't </span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">consistent</span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">. So, why </span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><i>should </i></span><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">they care?</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=660783#post660783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Never any answers&quot; is something that can be overdone, and I think this would be a case of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its the entire basis of the nWoD. There are no concrete answers by design. Mummy is the only game that deviates from this. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Especially as Castigation is in the blood, which implies the blood coming from a particular source. </div> </div> </div> The only implication is that the power is inherited. There's nothing to force the assumption that all Lucifuge come from the same source if the ST doesn't want to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> but saying they derive from many first causes that all happen manifest in the exact same way, and de facto coordinate with each other to keep the 666 total going, is vagueness, not mystery. </div> </div> </div> First of all, they DON'T manifest in the exact same way. Even if we assume Castigation 5 for all Lucifuge, there's a variety of powers that will show up. And that assumption is a stretch - many will have fewer powers than others. Secondly, Castigation is ritually invoked, and training can easily account for any similarities. Be wary of confirmation bias when making broad statements.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=660931#post660931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a variety of reasons why the Lucifuge's Castigations work on a larger group than just demons.</div> </div> </div> </div> Personally, I wonder if we will even have Infernal demons in 2e. I can't help but notice that the support for it has gone down significantly.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-12T14:17:48-07:00","id":662193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=661775#post661775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"> Curious minds inquiring - you feel the same way about the higher ups in the Conspiracies as well?</span><br /> <br /> <br /> Personally, I wonder if we will even have Infernal demons in 2e. I can't help but notice that the support for it has gone down significantly.</div> </div> </div> </div>0) MCN, you continue to be one of my favorites on the forums these days.<br /> <br /> 1) While I have favored theories(Board of Directors running an extradimensional Vigil) or pet theories(vampire Abe Lincoln and fate-twisting Loki leading Valkyrie) about the heads of the conspiracies, I make it a point not to speak for them. I have no clue what the limits of their knowledge and will not pretend to such until the story demands it-and then they know what the story tells me.<br /> <br /> Because what happens at the table is more fun than what happens in the forums.<br /> <br /> 2) Really the only blue book minor template to get acknowledged consistently is psychics and templates close enough to their form. I don't blame Onyx Path, given the sense and sensibility of their business model-it's really hard to follow up on ideas given the way things work, and often times Blue Books cover material that doesn't quite fit the rest of the World.<br /> <br /> That said, I imagine we'll see Infernal demons again given proper context and time, particularly as far as the Lucifuge go. While I'm not a huge fan of the Infernal Hegemony of the Burning Tree mentality of the fandom, I concede that using them as a very common base has a lot of merits, and I think Onyx Path will explore that in time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T03:21:29-07:00","id":662865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=661775#post661775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry, but I draw the line at &quot;the setting as presented is wrong!&quot; Do what you want with your games, say you prefer other things, but don't call the established setting wrong. The writers get to decide the setting and how things work. Not you.</div> </div> </div> </div>This I have to agree with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> First of all, they DON'T manifest in the exact same way. Even if we assume Castigation 5 for all Lucifuge, there's a variety of powers that will show up. And that assumption is a stretch - many will have fewer powers than others. Secondly, Castigation is ritually invoked, and training can easily account for any similarities. Be wary of confirmation bias when making broad statements. </div> </div> </div>Castigation is borne in the blood, and <i>not</i> all the powers are ritually invoked, some of them are simply on all the time. And we're using different definitions of manifest the same way; I mean the Lucifuges' blood-borne inheritance manifests in the same set of available powers, which revolve around the same themes of demoniacism, sin, and Hell.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=660931#post660931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a variety of reasons why the Lucifuge's Castigations work on a larger group than just demons.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not a question of what &quot;Castigations&quot; work on; only the abilities to or banish demons, where I think making them work only on demons would be worthwhile change. I mean no one expects the sunlight bomb in Advanced Armoury to work on anything besides vampires (and no one interprets its not doing so as Advanced Armoury only working on vampires).<br /> <br /> <br /> But none of this really matters until 2nd edition comes out, so I'll leave it there.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T04:27:25-07:00","id":662939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=658426#post658426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always ruled that Lucifuge abilities work on anything I would generally consider an 'outsider'. Inferno Demons, Spirits, Ghosts, Fae, Abyssal Entities, Supernal Creatures. Using them on Unchained and Angels has never come up in my game, but I don't see them as outsiders per se.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would limit term &quot;demon&quot; to the Lower Depths beings - Supernal Realms, even Pandemonium, are about platonic, ideal, perfect ( connected to virtue ) - it's all those things that are &quot;lower&quot; are &quot;demons ( hence the name LOWER Depths ). Inferno, True Fae, Abyssal and maybe Unchained can all be treated as &quot;demons&quot; then. Spirits and Ghosts could also, in some circumstances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T06:58:42-07:00","id":663042,"title":"","content":"Uh. . .just because something is perfected, Supernally speaking, doesn't mean it's connected to virtue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T07:04:37-07:00","id":663047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=662939#post662939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would limit term &quot;demon&quot; to the Lower Depths beings - Supernal Realms, even Pandemonium, are about platonic, ideal, perfect ( connected to virtue ) - it's all those things that are &quot;lower&quot; are &quot;demons ( hence the name LOWER Depths ). Inferno, True Fae, Abyssal and maybe Unchained can all be treated as &quot;demons&quot; then. Spirits and Ghosts could also, in some circumstances.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure why you're drawing such a relation between them just based on the perceived 'distance' of their realms to the supernal. That's not really what Lower Depths means, and the Supernal isn't necessarily about virtue. Most of the beings Hunters designate as demons also have no more overt link to the Supernal Realms than other supernatural phenomena, whether they have a clear adjacent arcana association or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 09-13-2015, 10:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T07:16:36-07:00","id":663106,"title":"","content":"I rather point that Lower Depths ( and similar phenomena, like Abyss ) are somehow &quot;hungry&quot; - Inferno needs feed on breaking virtue, True Fae are feeding on emotions and sanity, Abyss is feeding on the eating reality and corupting it's to it's means.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T07:56:45-07:00","id":663130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=662193#post662193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">0) MCN, you continue to be one of my favorites on the forums these days.</div> </div> </div> </div> Glad to of entertrainment, and thanks for the answers. <br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=662865#post662865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Castigation is borne in the blood, and <i>not</i> all the powers are ritually invoked, some of them are simply on all the time. And we're using different definitions of manifest the same way; I mean the Lucifuges' blood-borne inheritance manifests in the same set of available powers, which revolve around the same themes of demoniacism, sin, and Hell.</div> </div> </div> </div> And I stand by my statement - the powers manifest primarily through training. And that training can account for similarities. Further, while the story behind the powers generally invoke the themes of demons and sin, there are a significant number of abilities that just don't. The demon-control powers work on spirits and ghosts as easily as they do &quot;demons.&quot; Its a generic &quot;deal with ephemeral critters&quot; power set. Infernal visions actually has nothing to do with Hell. Hellfire is really just regular fire, nothing hellish about it. There's werewolf-like shapeshifting powers. Most of the powers that deal with sin are likely a matter of their job's focus as well. They're hunters that deal with both supernatural and mortal monsters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=662939#post662939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would limit term &quot;demon&quot; to the Lower Depths beings - Supernal Realms, even Pandemonium, are about platonic, ideal, perfect ( connected to virtue ) - it's all those things that are &quot;lower&quot; are &quot;demons ( hence the name LOWER Depths ). Inferno, True Fae, Abyssal and maybe Unchained can all be treated as &quot;demons&quot; then. Spirits and Ghosts could also, in some circumstances.</div> </div> </div> </div> Lower Depths is entirely a Mage description; I'm personally leery of using it to define demons across all game lines, especially when we have goetic demons as well as an Aeon based on the devil from Dante's Inferno as well as Supernal demons that were summoned. We also know that the Abyss isn't a Lower Depth realm, and that Castigation works on them. Also, not a term I'd apply to all the beings of Duat as well. There's some rather generous gods there. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=663106#post663106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I rather point that Lower Depths ( and similar phenomena, like Abyss ) are somehow &quot;hungry&quot; - Inferno needs feed on breaking virtue, True Fae are feeding on emotions and sanity, Abyss is feeding on the eating reality and corupting it's to it's means.</div> </div> </div> </div> Faerie isn't part of the Lower Depths, nor is the Abyss. The Lower Depths are places that are &quot;missing&quot; some of the Arcana as Mages describe them and hunger to fill it. That's not true of the fae (don't lack any of the Arcana) nor the abyss (who want to corrupt and devour reality for other reasons). As well, the strix are part of the lower depth, as they lack and hunger for Life.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T08:04:36-07:00","id":663145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=663130#post663130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Faerie isn't part of the Lower Depths, nor is the Abyss. The Lower Depths are places that are &quot;missing&quot; some of the Arcana as Mages describe them and hunger to fill it. That's not true of the fae (don't lack any of the Arcana) nor the abyss (who want to corrupt and devour reality for other reasons). As well, the strix are part of the lower depth, as they lack and hunger for Life.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is debatable. I remember reading somewhere that Faerie <b>is</b> in Lower Depths, according to <b>DaveB</b> - as to answer to &quot;Two Arcadias&quot; problem. And True Fae <b>are</b> missing one Arcana - Mind, the emotions and imagination they prey on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T08:08:04-07:00","id":663148,"title":"","content":"They thrive and define themselves by conflict, not emotions and imagination. And arguably, conflict between the Gentry does more to fulfill that than messing with mortals, at least based on Equinox Road.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T08:11:52-07:00","id":663151,"title":"","content":"Which arcarnum is the Inferno supposed to lack, anyway?<br /> <br /> Also I think if Faerie is indeed a Lower Depth there's an argument to be made for it being the one lacking Death, not Mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 09-13-2015, 11:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T08:27:30-07:00","id":663159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=663151#post663151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which arcarnum is the Inferno supposed to lack, anyway?<br /> <br /> Also I think if Faerie is indeed a Lower Depth there's an argument to be made for it being the one lacking Death, not Mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say Prime over Death.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T08:33:27-07:00","id":663162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=663151#post663151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which arcarnum is the Inferno supposed to lack, anyway?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind maybe?<br /> <br /> Anyway, no one has ever answered the question if Faerie is from the Lower Depths or not- maybe it is, maybe it isn't. Also, considering that the &quot;Lower Depths&quot; is the nickname mages has given to realms they don't understand and which seem to be resistant to their magic and that feed upon certain aspects of the world- which may be described by the Arcana, or be something more focused- Inferno eats Virtue, for example. Duat would also be classified as a Lower Depth because the Devourer eats Memories (which could be described as some sort of Time). Faerie also shows that trait by the fact that its denizens eats Creativity (which is symbolized by the fact that they can't create anything, and eat emotions and souls), so some mages may describe it as a Lower Depth, while others as something else (an Abyssal reflection of Arcadia, or some dark aspect of the Supernal Realm of Time and Fate, or maybe some place found in the Astral near the Primordial Dream?)<br /> <br /> This is also why the Depths and the Abyss are two different things- the Depths want to eat the world, while the Abyss wants to replace it. It reflects the symbols of the Supernal, twist them and break them apart, creating its own symbols out of them. It is a mirror which takes everything you hold dear and turn it into your biggest fear. Yes, it is mad and evil like the Depths- but the last you can at least understand. In order to understand the Abyss, you need to replace something in yourself with it- which mens becoming a little bit more mad in the process.<br /> <br /> In sort, the Abyss is not a Lower Depth, Faerie may be a Lower Depth and Castigations don't care at all about what mages say on the subject.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 09-13-2015, 11:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T09:44:04-07:00","id":663235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=662865#post662865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not a question of what &quot;Castigations&quot; work on; only the abilities to or banish demons, where I think making them work only on demons would be worthwhile change. I mean no one expects the sunlight bomb in Advanced Armoury to work on anything besides vampires (and no one interprets its not doing so as Advanced Armoury only working on vampires).<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but that's my point. The trio of power meant to work on demons(Summon/banish, bind, order), according to that sidebar, also work on Abyssal entities,spirits, faeries, or really any entity that's not from the material plane. That's not an accident, that's a deliberate design choice that works on a lot of levels most fans don't appreciate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-13-2015, 12:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T09:46:30-07:00","id":663236,"title":"","content":"Also worth noting: Th Lower Depths lacking in one or more of the Arcana is a strong theory, but it's not necessarily a confirmed theory. THe only thing that seems agreed on is &quot;It's off the map.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T10:16:21-07:00","id":663261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=663145#post663145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is debatable. I remember reading somewhere that Faerie <b>is</b> in Lower Depths, according to <b>DaveB</b> - as to answer to &quot;Two Arcadias&quot; problem.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm going to have to ask for a quote to back that up, because that doesn't sound like him. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=663236#post663236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also worth noting: Th Lower Depths lacking in one or more of the Arcana is a strong theory, but it's not necessarily a confirmed theory. THe only thing that seems agreed on is &quot;It's off the map.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> To be fair, the Lower Depths was originally a single realm of mana-hungry beings. Its evolved a lot since then. Well, the entire cosmology as a whole has, though Mage itself is still trapped in the oWoD 3-umbra model for some unusual reason. The 3 Umbra of the oWoD, plus the demonic beings trapped &quot;below&quot; the Underworld. The Lower Depths has kind of evolved since then to basically be a place where generic &quot;I-don't-know-shove-it-there!&quot; place. <br /> <br /> I think I heard David Brookshaw mention the missing-Arcana thing before as well, but lets be honest. Every non-human in the WoD is pretty much hungry to eat humans in some way. Spirits want human-essence, ghosts want human memory, goetics want human thought, strix want human bodies and life, and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T10:26:35-07:00","id":663262,"title":"","content":"I recall him saying that they're definitely not the same place, but that's as far as he went. <br /> <br /> For my part, I think it's an intriguingly plausible notion that I hadn't previously considered. And even if it's not true, figuring out where places fit in various cosmological models is a fun exercise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T11:51:51-07:00","id":663308,"title":"","content":"Mage 2E material we've seen is pretty consistent that the Supernal brings, as Symbols, reflect the nature of, but are not themselves, the Angels, Fae, Demons, Totem Beasts, or Shades that exist to be interacted with in the Fallen Cosmology, which may have their own Realms in said cosmology.<br /> <br /> So the relationship between Supernal Symbols of Fate and Time and the Gentry is effectively the same as the relationship between a given &quot;river&quot; you cross in your Awakening and an earthly body of water.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T21:12:38-07:00","id":663823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=663308#post663308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the relationship between Supernal Symbols of Fate and Time and the Gentry is effectively the same as the relationship between a given &quot;river&quot; you cross in your Awakening and an earthly body of water.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or &quot;nice story&quot;, Disney version fairies of Supernal, and wicked, mad True Fae. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T22:39:37-07:00","id":663900,"title":"","content":"On the &quot;when everything you have is a hammer&quot; issue, I'd say Hunters do care about correctly classifying monsters. However, due to the tangled and cryptic nature of the origins of monsters in the WoD, it is extremely difficult to get much more than basic info about, say, what kills a True Fae vs what kills a Beast. Besides, if you were a monster, and you knew Hunters existed, would you willingly give them info on how to hunt your own kind?<br /> <br /> However, Hunters simply don't have the time to know all the minutiae of monster taxonomy. Between the Vigil, their day jobs and their families, there's not much room for extensive research on Unchained Demons, Inferno Demons, Supernal Demons, Astral Demons and so on. Hunters are likely to make mistakes because they are often pressed for time, in addition to conflicting or similar information. Yeah, using holy water on a True Fae is likely to piss it off and make it attack the Hunter, even if holy water is not one of the True Fae's frailties. But if the Hunter was smart, he would have confronted the True Fae with one or more back up plans, and take note of how much damage the holy water apparently did. After reaching safety, the Hunter compares his experience with what he has been told. Hunters don't make the same mistake twice because doing that is virtually guaranteed to kill them.<br /> <br /> Were I to run a Hunter game, I wouldn't focus so much on the moral ambiguity of the Vigil. I'd focus on the sensation of being outmatched and having to work with the little intel you have about the enemy. Hunters aren't addicted to mysteries like Mages are because the former are not as flexibly equipped to explore the depths of the WoD (e.g. Integrity instead of Wisdom).<br /> <br /> In a nutshell: Hunters do make an effort to know what they're dealing with, but they can't do it all the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 09-14-2015, 04:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T23:52:07-07:00","id":663983,"title":"","content":"I'm endlessly amused by how often True Fae have come up in this thread as a thing that Hunters hunt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T00:16:07-07:00","id":664021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=663823#post663823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Or &quot;nice story&quot;, Disney version fairies of Supernal, and wicked, mad True Fae. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>You may be thinking the Supernal Symbols are friendlier than they are.<br /> <br /> Though, I'm not sure Disney faeries are that nice across the board either. Despite her friendly cgi straight-to-dvd incarnation, Tinkerbell of Peter Pan is pretty much a sociopath. She only regrets her plan to kill Wendy because it almost kills Peter. And of course, while the 3 good faeries are there, Maleficent herself is of faerie in Sleeping Beauty. The Blue Fairy of Pinnochio is pretty nice, but there was definitely something shady agenda going on on her Once Upon a Time incarnation... even if the show never intended that to be the case and thus never addressed it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T01:14:14-07:00","id":664043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=664021#post664021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You may be thinking the Supernal Symbols are friendlier than they are.<br /> <br /> Though, I'm not sure Disney faeries are that nice across the board either.</div> </div> </div> </div>They surely are more friendlier than mad pagan gods that Gentry are, don't you agree?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-14-2015, 04:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T02:46:18-07:00","id":664066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=663983#post663983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm endlessly amused by how often True Fae have come up in this thread as a thing that Hunters hunt.</div> </div> </div> </div> 1e incarnations of the Gentry were viable antagonists. 2e? Not so much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T04:54:13-07:00","id":664104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=664043#post664043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They surely are more friendlier than mad pagan gods that Gentry are, don't you agree?</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends on how friendly you consider the Exarchs. Or the Supernal Symbols for abuse, or murder, torture or unfriendliness. The Gentry, at least, don't really appreciate what it is they do. They can try to be friendly, it just comes out wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-14-2015, 08:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T05:44:06-07:00","id":664143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=663235#post663235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but that's my point. The trio of power meant to work on demons(Summon/banish, bind, order), according to that sidebar, also work on Abyssal entities, spirits, faeries, or really any entity that's not from the material plane. That's not an accident, that's a deliberate design choice that works on a lot of levels most fans don't appreciate.</div> </div> </div> </div>And <i>my</i> point is that I think it's worth changing that, because I think Hunter groups in particular benefit from being more specific in their setup. There's a difference between preferring a different choice to not understanding the one that was made.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=663236#post663236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also worth noting: The Lower Depths lacking in one or more of the Arcana is a strong theory, but it's not necessarily a confirmed theory. The only thing that seems agreed on is &quot;It's off the map.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. It's a logical theory for mages to adopt, and mages are the only ones who study this stuff by and large (which lends some weight to their theories - people who study stuff tend to understand it better than people who don't - but hardly absolute weight). And even if it's technically true, it may still not be the most <i>useful</i> way to understand what a realm lacks.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T06:28:59-07:00","id":664207,"title":"","content":"Well then, we're at an impasse. I disliked the later conspiracies for being more specific.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T08:43:50-07:00","id":664347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=664143#post664143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And <i>my</i> point is that I think it's worth changing that, because I think Hunter groups in particular benefit from being more specific in their setup. There's a difference between preferring a different choice to not understanding the one that was made.</div> </div> </div> </div> Why would you think its worth changing? That would make Endowments worthless in a vast number of games. The ST would have to decide on single supernaturals to hunt, and then exclude any others. Or just go with tier 1/2 hunting. I'm really at a loss why you'd want to make the core 6 ineffective against the majority of supernaturals.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T12:03:54-07:00","id":664591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=664347#post664347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Why would you think its worth changing? That would make Endowments worthless in a vast number of games. The ST would have to decide on single supernaturals to hunt, and then exclude any others. Or just go with tier 1/2 hunting. I'm really at a loss why you'd want to make the core 6 ineffective against the majority of supernaturals.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes no sense. I think Hunter groups benefit from specificity in their design rather than being ad-hoc types - eg, when the material for both Lucifuge and Casitgation says it's because they have the blood of demons, I think demons should mean demons, not just the blood any old otherworldly entity - and yes, I think that means Castigation powers described as working on demons should work on demons rather than any old otherworldly entity. But that's what, two or three of them? How the hell does this translate into making Castigation as a whole useless against the majority of supernaturals?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T13:35:25-07:00","id":664699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=664347#post664347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Why would you think its worth changing? That would make Endowments worthless in a vast number of games.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with SunlessNick. That really doesn't make sense.<br /> <br /> Not only does it fail to make Castigation as a whole useless against the majority of supernaturals, summoning and ordering around a demon <b>is </b>useful against all supernaturals. Getting a demon to attack your enemy is a useful ability against just about anyone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T13:56:42-07:00","id":664717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=664066#post664066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> 1e incarnations of the Gentry were viable antagonists. 2e? Not so much.</div> </div> </div> </div> Why? Did you read that on a new open dev spoiler? What changes do they plan on making that will make the Gentry less viable as antagonists?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T14:25:32-07:00","id":664775,"title":"","content":"Two things.<br /> <br /> 1) In line with the story of Changeling, a lot of emphasis has been placed on making the True Fae feel like the Big Bad again. A large part of this is shifting the active presence of them onto Huntsmen and Loyalists, while letting them <i>be</i> the story in the background. True Fae are now emphasized to be rare, and when you meet them, they're terrifying to come across. Your instinct should be to run, not fight. How is this done? What's keeping the True Fae from just sweeping in? Well, why you don't want to fight hasn't been brought up yet, so mum on that. But how do they just not sweep in?<br /> <br /> 2)This comes to a thing that didn't come across in the original writeup of the Court System, as I found out with Dave while making Los Angeles's Courts, so I figure now's as good a time as any to bring it up.<br /> <br /> So, you know how there are Approaches Huntsmen can take to gain Yearnings, whatever that is? Well, they can do that, but they don't have to.<br /> <br /> The True Fae don't have that luxury. They <i>must</i> go by the Approaches when they enter into a Freehold's territory. They must fulfill every single one that is involved with going after someone.<br /> <br /> Los Angeles has four Approaches, one for the freehold, one for each court. Paris has <i>ten</i> Approaches, two for each court. Can you imagine how much tripping over existential laws can happen with that?<br /> <br /> Yeah, no one wants to deal with that, which is why they send in Huntsmen and Loyalists first to break down the Bulwark.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 09-14-2015, 05:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T14:33:10-07:00","id":664784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=664699#post664699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with SunlessNick. That really doesn't make sense.<br /> <br /> Not only does it fail to make Castigation as a whole useless against the majority of supernaturals, summoning and ordering around a demon <b>is </b>useful against all supernaturals. Getting a demon to attack your enemy is a useful ability against just about anyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Insert everything else I've been saying.<br /> <br /> Something else to consider is that by closing the book on other options, you close the book on the mystery of Lady Lucifuge. Lots of time and energy is dedicated in the books to what she might be, with Mortal Remains suggesting at least three directions in that alone. By leaving the book open, you keep the question of whether or not she's jerking everyone's chains around or not alive and well. Considering this is a big enough deal that one of the three factions is dedicated to figuring this shit out, I'd say it's time you opened the grimoire and smelled the fairy dust and brimstone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T00:35:25-07:00","id":665437,"title":"","content":"Everything else you've been saying is about fluff and thematics. I was saying that a power to summon and order an Infernal demon would be useful when hunting non-infernal monsters.<br /> <br /> And remember - while I'd prefer it otherwise, I'm basically ok with your desire for Castigation to work on more than just demons, so long as an actual explenation was given for why it works. The True Fae could be summoning the ones tithed to hell. The Abyss could be summoning prisoners of war from hell. Etc etc.<br /> <br /> (Though I would be disapoionted if the 2E anti-Mage Castigations go for an Abyss based power before they go for a sin-of-pride/hubris based power) <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=664784#post664784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something else to consider is that by closing the book on other options, you close the book on the mystery of Lady Lucifuge.</div> </div> </div> </div> I disagree. Even if every signal Lucifuge PC is descended from the Inferno; Lady Lucifuge could still be an exception.<br /> <br /> God Machine angels, True Fae, Qashmallim, Archmages, Abrahamic angels, etc. You know what they all have in common? They're all powerful enough and flexible enough that they could disguise themselves as a &quot;mortal who inhereted powers from Infernal blood&quot; and fool whatever &quot;detect Infernal&quot; Castigations the Lucifuge might have.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T04:25:10-07:00","id":665518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=664591#post664591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That makes no sense. I think Hunter groups benefit from specificity in their design rather than being ad-hoc types - eg, when the material for both Lucifuge and Casitgation says it's because they have the blood of demons, I think demons should mean demons, not just the blood any old otherworldly entity - and yes, I think that means Castigation powers described as working on demons should work on demons rather than any old otherworldly entity. But that's what, two or three of them? How the hell does this translate into making Castigation as a whole useless against the majority of supernaturals?</div> </div> </div> </div> Because the implications of your statement goes beyond just Castigation. Imagine if TFV's ethereal bullets only hit ghosts. On a hunt, the PCs find a haunted house. Except, its actually a death spirit. The bullets are worthless, and 9 times out of 10, hunters aren't equipped to be able to tell the difference between a ghost and a death-themed spirit. Or an angel. Having to be highly specific is detrimental to the game, because it requires you to be highly specific on identifying the monster you hunt, and hunters just aren't equipped for that. <br /> <br /> Castigation being reduced to just &quot;infernal demons&quot; hurts the Lucifuge because the game moves from being able to deal with a demonic ghost. Unless you get the Summon power or face another demon, the ability to bind or command demons becomes worthless. And not everyone that takes those powers wants to be a summoner. And, again, it requires you to accurately identify the difference between an evil ghost, a wicked spirit, a depraved angelic Mission, an Abyssal entity, a rogue goetic, and something actually infernally tainted.<br /> <br /> And so on. Being highly specific means that you can't use your abilities out of highly specific situations, which is a poor way to design powers. And that's just from a mechanical design stand point - ArcaneArts touched on thematic aspects of it as well. The game is about standing vigil against the monsters in the night and fighting back. The game does not revolve around studying and identifying classifications - that's Mage. Or arguably Beast. The entire game's focuses are different, and you want the mechanics to support the game's themes and not force it into another direction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=665437#post665437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree. Even if every signal Lucifuge PC is descended from the Inferno; Lady Lucifuge could still be an exception.</div> </div> </div> </div> Which is still a shoehorn. If you go with &quot;She's really another supernatural!&quot; that forces your mystery to go in specific directions. Which is more limited than what we have now - we can do both what you suggest, and far more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T05:43:40-07:00","id":665571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=665518#post665518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And so on. Being highly specific means that you can't use your abilities out of highly specific situations, which is a poor way to design powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, sure, if you completely exaggerate what I said beyond anything I stated or implied, then your point would stand.<br /> <br /> To expand on this some:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Imagine if TFV's ethereal bullets only hit ghosts. </div> </div> </div>The entire rationale for how and why etheric bullets work doesn't revolve around ghosts in particular. The entire rationale for how and why Call the Pit and Mandate of Hell work <i>does</i> revolve around demonic heredity in particular. So your example doesn't even vaguely follow from mine. And to reuse a previous example, why don't have a problem with TFV's sunlight bomb thing only working on vampires? By your logic, it would be more appropriate for it to affect all &quot;creatures of darkness.&quot;<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Castigation being reduced to just &quot;infernal demons&quot; hurts the Lucifuge because the game moves from being able to deal with a demonic ghost. </div> </div> </div>Once again, Call the Pit and Mandate of Hell does not equal Castigation. Continuing to make this conflation isn't helping your argument.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ArcaneArts touched on thematic aspects of it as well. </div> </div> </div>As long as we're talking theme, the entire theme of the Lucifuge and Castigation - not just what the powers do, but what effect having them has on the hunter - revolves around sin, punishment, with a dash of repentence and redemption, a heritage that's absolutely to be feared, and a heritage of authority. Those things fit Hell (in various sorts) very well. They only fit narrow slices of, say, ghostly ancestors prehuman giants, pagan gods, or faeries; shoehorning those things into the Lucifuge's ancestry shortchanges their thematic potential.<br /> <br /> Like it or not, Call the Pit and Mandate of Hell working on all otherworldly entities is the odd thing out in the game material. It makes more sense to treat them as such than the everything else. It makes more sense to change them than everything else.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":321,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","user":"SunlessNick","date":". 09-15-2015, 12:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T09:56:44-07:00","id":665827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=665518#post665518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Because the implications of your statement goes beyond just Castigation. Imagine if TFV's ethereal bullets only hit ghosts. On a hunt, the PCs find a haunted house. Except, its actually a death spirit. The bullets are worthless, and 9 times out of 10, hunters aren't equipped to be able to tell the difference between a ghost and a death-themed spirit. Or an angel. Having to be highly specific is detrimental to the game, because it requires you to be highly specific on identifying the monster you hunt, and hunters just aren't equipped for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's exactly what I want from a Hunter game. I want the majority of each hunt to be about researching and identifying your foe, and I want the consiquences of getting the research wrong and going in with the wrong weapons to be deadly.<br /> <br /> Now maybe TF:V should be the exception. The Hunter Org for players who want to just kick in doors and shoot monsters; but in general - see above.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T10:58:57-07:00","id":665897,"title":"","content":"personally, while I do think that doing research (and the consequences of research going wrong) should be a defining part of being an hunter, I do believe that Hunter shouldn't force itself around the cosmologies of other gamelines- that is, even if &quot;holy water&quot; shouldn't usually work on vampires, the MM may have found a way to make it work, no matter how weird it may be from a vampire's point of view. I think it is quit possible to find a middle ground between the two points of view (for example, most of the &quot;cosmology bending&quot; abilities should be formed as Endowments), but one shouldn't step on the toes of the other. If research means nothing, than the huge libraries of the Loyalists, the detailed demonic hierarchies of the Lucifuge and the ancient writings of the AKD means nothing. If Hunter won't break away from how the WoD is defined in other books, it won't have a true identity of its own, and would really turn into a &quot;blue book supplement&quot;- something that I personally would really hate to see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T11:32:02-07:00","id":665932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=665897#post665897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">personally, while I do think that doing research (and the consequences of research going wrong) should be a defining part of being an hunter, I do believe that Hunter shouldn't force itself around the cosmologies of other gamelines- that is, even if &quot;holy water&quot; shouldn't usually work on vampires, the MM may have found a way to make it work, no matter how weird it may be from a vampire's point of view. I think it is quit possible to find a middle ground between the two points of view (for example, most of the &quot;cosmology bending&quot; abilities should be formed as Endowments), but one shouldn't step on the toes of the other. If research means nothing, than the huge libraries of the Loyalists, the detailed demonic hierarchies of the Lucifuge and the ancient writings of the AKD means nothing. If Hunter won't break away from how the WoD is defined in other books, it won't have a true identity of its own, and would really turn into a &quot;blue book supplement&quot;- something that I personally would really hate to see.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I'm fine with MM having holy water that &quot;works&quot;, but it should be an endowment that works on holy water and thereafter makes that holy water &quot;work&quot;. But it's not really the holy water that does it, it's the Benediction.<br /> <br /> There's pretty much two options as far as I'm concerned: either Hunter conforms to the World of Darkness' cosmology, or it takes place in it's own universe like Scion does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T12:00:19-07:00","id":665951,"title":"","content":"or that Hunter would &quot;add&quot; things to the WoD, just like other gamelines do. When Changeling does something weird in the Astral which is against what mages think possible, no one complains. When Hunter says that certain powers don't care about the origin of certain entity, everyone start raging like it slaughtered their favorite puppy. The World of Darkness is a weird place- Hunter just shows how much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T12:37:12-07:00","id":665972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=665571#post665571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, sure, if you completely exaggerate what I said beyond anything I stated or implied, then your point would stand.</div> </div> </div> </div> Its a natural implication of what you said. You wanted to talk about being specific in terms of powers. I went with examples of the implications of being specific. From a game design standpoint, it just doesn't work well as character powers. Its unnecessarily limiting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The entire rationale for how and why etheric bullets work doesn't revolve around ghosts in particular. The entire rationale for how and why Call the Pit and Mandate of Hell work <i>does</i> revolve around demonic heredity in particular. So your example doesn't even vaguely follow from mine. </div> </div> </div> It was an example of how being unnecessarily specific can be a poor choice from a game design standpoint. As a mechanic, its pretty bad for a number of reasons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And to reuse a previous example, why don't have a problem with TFV's sunlight bomb thing only working on vampires? By your logic, it would be more appropriate for it to affect all &quot;creatures of darkness.&quot; </div> </div> </div> I presume you're talking about hte VDSB (victim detonated sun bomb) on page 154. If so, then it DOES work on non-vamps. Against vampires, it provokes a fear frenzy. That's using fake light to trigger an innate bane of vampires. Against everyone else, it works like a glorified flash grenade. Because all its doing is shooting out artificial light, after all. People are reacting as appropriate to a giant flash of bright light in their face. If there was another kind of supernatural that had a bane or some kind of weakness to bright light, then they'd be reacting as appropriate as well.<br /> <br /> The bomb is triggered by a being with core temperature below 94 F. If a lizard man with a core temperature of 87 walked on the scene, he could just as easily trigger the bomb as well as the vampire. And its also goes off when a random room temperature objects, like a ball, crosses the line.<br /> <br /> So, yeah. Bad example. It does work on everyone. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Once again, Call the Pit and Mandate of Hell does not equal Castigation. Continuing to make this conflation isn't helping your argument. </div> </div> </div> You are the one who brought them up in the first place as the ones that specifically call out demons. Furthermore, its just an example, I never said it was the whole of Castigation. Who's the one exaggerating what I said beyond anything I stated or implied now?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As long as we're talking theme, the entire theme of the Lucifuge and Castigation - not just what the powers do, but what effect having them has on the hunter - revolves around sin, punishment, with a dash of repentence and redemption, a heritage that's absolutely to be feared, and a heritage of authority. Those things fit Hell (in various sorts) very well. They only fit narrow slices of, say, ghostly ancestors prehuman giants, pagan gods, or faeries; shoehorning those things into the Lucifuge's ancestry shortchanges their thematic potential. </div> </div> </div> One. There are no &quot;pagan gods&quot; in the WoD. That's not a classification of any kind. You have beings that are misidentified by independant viewers as a god, but actually aren't. And, if we're talking about independant viewers, its entirely in theme for those with an Abrahamic view point to classify &quot;pagan god&quot; - like beings as demons or saints/angels. The Abrahamic faiths are full of examples of doing just that.<br /> <br /> Two, that narrow slice are the beings that hunters tend to encounter. They're hunting the monsters, and the nice spirits aren't the ones that are being encountered. The Gentry have been called demons. People often call a lot of things demons. Prehuman giants, like Titans from Greek myth who are trapped in a caged pit by the Divine... sounds a lot like Hell. A lot of the stuff you're naming has been called &quot;demons&quot; before.<br /> <br /> Three, &quot;A Heritage of Authority.&quot; Your own words. Why <i>shouldn't</i> hell have rulership over others? Its a common perception in Christianity that this world is controlled by the devil. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Like it or not, Call the Pit and Mandate of Hell working on all otherworldly entities is the odd thing out in the game material </div> </div> </div> Like it or not, it makes perfect sense, espceially when you consider the very nature of the infernal and how it corrupts everything it touches. Sorry, but I don't think its odd at all,. Not from a story point of view, not from a mechanics point of view.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T12:38:13-07:00","id":665973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=665932#post665932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's pretty much two options as far as I'm concerned: either Hunter conforms to the World of Darkness' cosmology, or it takes place in it's own universe like Scion does.</div> </div> </div> </div> The problem is that there ISN'T a WoD cosmology that you can easily map. There's nothign to conform to, because its a giant ??? pasted over the vast majority of it. We know there's the material world, the Hisil, the Astral, the Underworld, the Hedge. Everything else is a big question mark. We also know that the five realms interact somehow - the God Machine gears are in the Hedge. There are faeries in the Underworld. Ghosts in the Hisil. Spirits in the Astral. Goetics and tulpa form in the material. So, why shouldn't there be great big web of craziness when we add more stuff in?<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: Here's the thing. The WoD is specifically designed so you can't fit everything into nice easy boxes. Castigation and its everything-is-a-demon stance is merely an extension of that basic philosophy. Trying to shoehorn everything &quot;demon&quot; into an Infernal box, when the Infernal itself is undefined even in its own book, just doesn't work.<br /> <br /> Sure, it makes sense from an individual story perspective.. if you want to tell that story. From a design perspective where you want to have as many story possibilities as you can make, its terrible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 09-15-2015, 03:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T16:29:04-07:00","id":666134,"title":"","content":"MCN: sorry, might have used the wrong word there, but I was referring to things like &quot;how Vampirism works&quot; and so forth rather than how the various Realms Invisible function in the greater scheme of things.<br /> <br /> Edit: specifically, if Hunter2 wants to, say, speak on Vampires and point to things in Requiem, it needs to follow Requiem's fluff. It's fine, even, to be like &quot;here are some rules for DIFFERENT vampires, because the ones in Requiem aren't the only ones out there!&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":274,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","user":"Enokh","date":". 09-15-2015, 07:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T07:33:48-07:00","id":666964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/655261-lucifuge-s-demons-and-a-2e-update-question?p=665972#post665972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its a natural implication of what you said. You wanted to talk about being specific in terms of powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>You misunderstood me. I said being specific in their <i>setup</i> - what they are and where they come from. Following through on powers that are explicitly designed in terms of a particular origin follows through on that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I never said it was the whole of Castigation. Who's the one exaggerating what I said beyond anything I stated or implied now? </div> </div> </div>Yes you did:<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/